# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets — never committed.
#
# `.env` is where a real OPENAI_API_KEY lives. `.env.example` is the template
# and IS committed, which is why the negation below is not optional: a bare
# `.env*` pattern would silently swallow the template and leave reviewers with
# no documentation of the configuration at all.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Databases. WAL leaves -wal and -shm sidecars that preserve state on their own,
# so the glob matters — deleting only `alert_router.db` does not reset anything.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
alert_router.db*
scenario_*.db*
verify_module*.db*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
